spec: specs/openapi.md stage 3

why: the last open stage of the operator's OpenAPI ask, and the only
  one that needs no decision from anyone. Every operation in the
  published document is identified by a DERIVED id and nothing else:
  `getEventsByEmail` says what the url is, never what the operation is
  for. The media lane gave each ANSWER a sentence; the operation still
  has none.

what: an entry may carry a summary. One builder method on `Router`
  rather than a parameter on twenty combinators: `.summarised("...")`
  attaches to the entry just declared, which is what a builder chain
  already reads as. The renderer emits `summary`; the page shows it.
  And `out`/`outAt`/`jsonOut`/`jsonOutAt` gain the `description` the
  media combinators already take, so an answer stops reading "the
  declared answer".

then the consumer: okay-demo's six operations summarised, its
  committed document regenerated, and a test that every operation in
  the published document has one — the same shape as the guard that
  keeps `undeclared` out.

not in scope: tags, external docs, a long `description` per operation,
  an operationId override. Each is a separate consumer's ask.

next: Entry.summary + Router.summarised, then the renderer
